{
  "body_human_readable": "### \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Film Finances: A Look at the Numbers\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction series, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to achieve a worldwide box office gross of approximately $104.5 million.\n\nThe film, directed by Garth Jennings, was released in the United Kingdom on April 28, 2005, and a day later in North America. In its opening weekend in North America, it secured the top spot at the box office with earnings of $21.1 million. The worldwide box office total was comprised of $51,085,416 from the domestic market and $53,393,000 from international markets. Despite earning back its production budget, the film's performance was not considered strong enough to warrant a sequel.",
